### 1. **src/valkey-benchmark.c:392** — RDMA event loop bypass breaks all RDMA benchmark traffic
```c
if (config.rdma) {
    writeHandler(el, c->context->fd, c, 0); /* RDMA context always writable, but it can't be invoked by AE_WRITABLE */
} else {
    aeCreateFileEvent(el, c->context->fd, AE_WRITABLE, writeHandler, c);
}
```
**Failure scenario**: Run `valkey-benchmark --rdma -t set`. The first `writeHandler` call executes once at client creation, sends one pipeline batch, then **never runs again** because no `AE_WRITABLE` event is registered. Benchmark hangs after initial requests, reporting near-zero throughput.

---

### 2. **src/valkey-benchmark.c:819** — Same event loop bypass in `createClient` initial connection
```c
if (config.idlemode == 0) {
    if (config.rdma) {
        writeHandler(el, c->context->fd, c, 0);
    } else {
        aeCreateFileEvent(el, c->context->fd, AE_WRITABLE, writeHandler, c);
    }
}
```
**Failure scenario**: Same as above — RDMA benchmark clients send one burst then stall permanently.

